  "question": {
    "text": "Both the diodes used in the circuit shown are assumed to be ideal and have negligible resistance when these are forward biased. Built in potential in each diode is <math><mn>0.7</mn><mi></mi><mi>V</mi></math>. For the input voltages shown in the figure, the voltage (in Volts) at point A is ________<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0156_5ec90d832688.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 155px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0156_730b4a0a4fb7.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 146px;\" /><br />Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Right diode is reversed baised and left diode is forward biased<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.7</mn></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> Volt"
  }
